IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `snap-core`
IMPORT `snap1-logic`
IMPORT `snap1-s2014-e2`

-- 7 U.S.C. 2014(g): allowable financial resources.
-- SOURCE: usc07-ch51.txt (a converter's rendering, not the official text).
-- Seams taken as inputs: s 2012(j) (the household includes an elderly or disabled member); the regulations in force on 1 June 1982 (paragraph (2)(A));
-- s 2015(d) and s 2025(h)(1)(F) (a plan for self-sufficiency, paragraph (3)).
-- THE TOTAL IS A PAIR: the text itself says only some resources are included, and sends the rest to regulations that are not among the sources.
-- So a resource is counted as shown to count (the text includes it), or as one that may count (the text neither includes nor excludes it); the caller never reads
-- "not shown to be included" as "not included".

§ `s 2014(g)(1) The limit`

-- src:380 | The Secretary shall prescribe the types and allowable amounts of financial resources (liquid and nonliquid assets) an eligible household may own, and shall, in so doing, assure that a household otherwise eligible to participate in the supplemental nutrition assistance program will not be eligible to participate if its resources exceed $2,000 (as adjusted in accordance with subparagraph (B)), or, in the case of a household which consists of or includes an elderly or disabled member, if its resources exceed $3,000 (as adjusted in accordance with subparagraph (B)).
@ref s 2014(g)(1)(A), the limit (src:380)
GIVEN `the value of the resources shown to count, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the value of the resources that may count, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the limit, as adjusted, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2014(g)(1)(A) the resources exceed the limit` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the value of the resources shown to count, in dollars` GREATER THAN `the limit, as adjusted, in dollars`
            THEN JUST TRUE  -- the text says yes: "will not be eligible to participate if its resources exceed $2,000 (as adjusted in accordance with subparagraph (B))"
        IF `the value of the resources that may count, in dollars` AT MOST `the limit, as adjusted, in dollars`
            THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "will not be eligible to participate if its resources exceed" the limit (a failed "if", marginal reading (a))
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the resources that are neither included nor excluded by the text count is for regulations not among the sources

-- src:380 | The Secretary shall prescribe the types and allowable amounts of financial resources (liquid and nonliquid assets) an eligible household may own, and shall, in so doing, assure that a household otherwise eligible to participate in the supplemental nutrition assistance program will not be eligible to participate if its resources exceed $2,000 (as adjusted in accordance with subparagraph (B)), or, in the case of a household which consists of or includes an elderly or disabled member, if its resources exceed $3,000 (as adjusted in accordance with subparagraph (B)).
@ref s 2014(g)(1)(A), which limit (src:380)
GIVEN `the value of the resources shown to count, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the value of the resources that may count, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `s 2012(j) the household includes an elderly or disabled member` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the limit for a household with no elderly or disabled member, as adjusted, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the limit for a household with an elderly or disabled member, as adjusted, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2014(g)(1)(A) the household is ineligible because its resources exceed the limit` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `snap1 is definitely yes` `s 2012(j) the household includes an elderly or disabled member`
            THEN `s 2014(g)(1)(A) the resources exceed the limit` `the value of the resources shown to count, in dollars` `the value of the resources that may count, in dollars` `the limit for a household with an elderly or disabled member, as adjusted, in dollars`
        IF `snap1 is definitely no` `s 2012(j) the household includes an elderly or disabled member`
            THEN `s 2014(g)(1)(A) the resources exceed the limit` `the value of the resources shown to count, in dollars` `the value of the resources that may count, in dollars` `the limit for a household with no elderly or disabled member, as adjusted, in dollars`
        IF `s 2014(g)(1)(A) the resources exceed the limit` `the value of the resources shown to count, in dollars` `the value of the resources that may count, in dollars` `the limit for a household with an elderly or disabled member, as adjusted, in dollars`
           EQUALS `s 2014(g)(1)(A) the resources exceed the limit` `the value of the resources shown to count, in dollars` `the value of the resources that may count, in dollars` `the limit for a household with no elderly or disabled member, as adjusted, in dollars`
            THEN `s 2014(g)(1)(A) the resources exceed the limit` `the value of the resources shown to count, in dollars` `the value of the resources that may count, in dollars` `the limit for a household with no elderly or disabled member, as adjusted, in dollars`  -- both limits give the same answer, so the unknown does not matter
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the household includes an elderly or disabled member was not supplied, and the answer differs between the two limits

-- src:380 | The Secretary shall prescribe the types and allowable amounts of financial resources (liquid and nonliquid assets) an eligible household may own, and shall, in so doing, assure that a household otherwise eligible to participate in the supplemental nutrition assistance program will not be eligible to participate if its resources exceed $2,000 (as adjusted in accordance with subparagraph (B)), or, in the case of a household which consists of or includes an elderly or disabled member, if its resources exceed $3,000 (as adjusted in accordance with subparagraph (B)).
@ref s 2014(g)(1)(A), the limit in force (src:380)
GIVEN `the fiscal year` IS A NUMBER
      `s 2012(j) the household includes an elderly or disabled member` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 2014(g)(1) the resource limit for the household` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the fiscal year` EQUALS 2027)
            THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): only the fiscal year 2027 limits were supplied; every October 1 the amounts are adjusted for the Consumer Price Index
        IF `snap1 is definitely yes` `s 2012(j) the household includes an elderly or disabled member`
            THEN JUST `s 2014(g)(1) resource limit for a household with an elderly or disabled member, FY 2027`
        IF `snap1 is definitely no` `s 2012(j) the household includes an elderly or disabled member`
            THEN JUST `s 2014(g)(1) resource limit for all other households, FY 2027`
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the household includes an elderly or disabled member was not supplied

-- src:383 | Beginning on October 1, 2008, and each October 1 thereafter, the amounts specified in subparagraph (A) shall be adjusted and rounded down to the nearest $250 increment to reflect changes for the 12-month period ending the preceding June in the Consumer Price Index for All Urban Consumers
@ref s 2014(g)(1)(B)(i), the unrounded amount (src:383)
GIVEN `the unrounded amount for the prior 12-month period, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the change for the 12-month period ending the preceding June in the Consumer Price Index for All Urban Consumers, as a fraction` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 2014(g)(1)(B)(i) the adjusted amount before rounding` MEANS
    `the unrounded amount for the prior 12-month period, in dollars` TIMES (1 PLUS `the change for the 12-month period ending the preceding June in the Consumer Price Index for All Urban Consumers, as a fraction`)

-- src:383 | Beginning on October 1, 2008, and each October 1 thereafter, the amounts specified in subparagraph (A) shall be adjusted and rounded down to the nearest $250 increment to reflect changes for the 12-month period ending the preceding June in the Consumer Price Index for All Urban Consumers published by the Bureau of Labor Statistics of the Department of Labor.
@ref s 2014(g)(1)(B)(i), the rounding (src:383)
GIVEN `the adjusted amount before rounding, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 2014(g)(1)(B)(i) the adjusted amount rounded down to the nearest $250 increment` MEANS
    250 TIMES FLOOR (`the adjusted amount before rounding, in dollars` DIVIDED BY 250)

-- src:385 | Each adjustment under clause (i) shall be based on the unrounded amount for the prior 12-month period.
@ref s 2014(g)(1)(B)(ii), requirement (src:385)
GIVEN `the adjustment was computed from the unrounded amount for the prior 12-month period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2014(g)(1)(B)(ii) the adjustment conforms` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the adjustment was computed from the unrounded amount for the prior 12-month period`
            THEN JUST TRUE  -- the text says yes: "shall be based on the unrounded amount for the prior 12-month period"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text requires the unrounded base and does not say what follows from a rounded one

-- ONE RESOURCE AS THE HOUSEHOLD HOLDS IT. The two answers are the text's, taken from the functions of paragraphs (2) to (8): NOTHING is "the text does not say".
DECLARE `s 2014(g) resource` HAS
    `s 2014(g) the value of the resource if it counts, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
    `s 2014(g) whether the text includes the resource`             IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `s 2014(g) whether the text excludes the resource`             IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN

-- An exclusion decides over an inclusion, because every exclusion paragraph says "shall exclude" or "shall not be included" of a named class,
-- and (g)(6)(B) itself speaks of resources "excluded under another paragraph of this subsection" (fork F-G1: a savings account in a retirement plan).
-- src:380 | The Secretary shall prescribe the types and allowable amounts of financial resources (liquid and nonliquid assets) an eligible household may own, and shall, in so doing, assure that a household otherwise eligible to participate in the supplemental nutrition assistance program will not be eligible to participate if its resources exceed $2,000 (as adjusted in accordance with subparagraph (B)), or, in the case of a household which consists of or includes an elderly or disabled member, if its resources exceed $3,000 (as adjusted in accordance with subparagraph (B)).
@ref s 2014(g)(1), the resources shown to count (src:380)
GIVEN resource IS A `s 2014(g) resource`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 2014(g)(1) the value of the resource that is shown to count` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `snap1 is definitely yes` (resource's `s 2014(g) whether the text excludes the resource`) THEN 0
        IF `snap1 is definitely yes` (resource's `s 2014(g) whether the text includes the resource`) THEN resource's `s 2014(g) the value of the resource if it counts, in dollars`
        OTHERWISE 0

-- src:380 | The Secretary shall prescribe the types and allowable amounts of financial resources (liquid and nonliquid assets) an eligible household may own, and shall, in so doing, assure that a household otherwise eligible to participate in the supplemental nutrition assistance program will not be eligible to participate if its resources exceed $2,000 (as adjusted in accordance with subparagraph (B)), or, in the case of a household which consists of or includes an elderly or disabled member, if its resources exceed $3,000 (as adjusted in accordance with subparagraph (B)).
@ref s 2014(g)(1), the resources that may count (src:380)
GIVEN resource IS A `s 2014(g) resource`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 2014(g)(1) the value of the resource that may count` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `snap1 is definitely yes` (resource's `s 2014(g) whether the text excludes the resource`) THEN 0
        IF `snap1 is definitely no` (resource's `s 2014(g) whether the text includes the resource`) THEN 0
        OTHERWISE resource's `s 2014(g) the value of the resource if it counts, in dollars`

GIVEN resources IS A LIST OF `s 2014(g) resource`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 2014(g)(1) the total value of the resources shown to count` MEANS
    sum (map (GIVEN resource YIELD `s 2014(g)(1) the value of the resource that is shown to count` resource) resources)

GIVEN resources IS A LIST OF `s 2014(g) resource`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 2014(g)(1) the total value of the resources that may count` MEANS
    sum (map (GIVEN resource YIELD `s 2014(g)(1) the value of the resource that may count` resource) resources)

§ `s 2014(g)(2) Included assets`

-- src:388 | Subject to the other provisions of this paragraph, the Secretary shall, in prescribing inclusions in, and exclusions from, financial resources, follow the regulations in force as of June 1, 1982 (other than those relating to licensed vehicles and inaccessible resources).
@ref s 2014(g)(2)(A), the regulations of 1 June 1982 (src:388)
GIVEN `the resource is a licensed vehicle` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the resource is an inaccessible resource` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the regulations in force as of June 1, 1982 include the resource in financial resources` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2014(g)(2)(A) the resource is included in financial resources by the regulations in force as of June 1, 1982` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the resource is a licensed vehicle` OR `the resource is an inaccessible resource`
            THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the regulations of 1 June 1982 are followed "other than those relating to licensed vehicles and inaccessible resources"
        OTHERWISE `the regulations in force as of June 1, 1982 include the resource in financial resources`  -- the answer of an instrument that is not among the sources, taken as an input

-- src:391 | (i) any boat, snowmobile, or airplane used for recreational purposes;
@ref s 2014(g)(2)(B)(i) (src:391)
GIVEN `the resource is a boat, snowmobile, or airplane` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the resource is used for recreational purposes` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2014(g)(2)(B)(i) the resource is included in financial resources` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the resource is a boat, snowmobile, or airplane` AND `the resource is used for recreational purposes`
            THEN JUST TRUE  -- the text says yes: "The Secretary shall include in financial resources— (i) any boat, snowmobile, or airplane used for recreational purposes"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the clause names a class and does not say that a resource outside it is not included

-- src:392 | (ii) any vacation home;
@ref s 2014(g)(2)(B)(ii) (src:392)
GIVEN `the resource is a vacation home` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2014(g)(2)(B)(ii) the resource is included in financial resources` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the resource is a vacation home`
            THEN JUST TRUE  -- the text says yes: "The Secretary shall include in financial resources— (ii) any vacation home"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the clause names a class and does not say that a resource outside it is not included

-- src:393 | (iii) any mobile home used primarily for vacation purposes;
@ref s 2014(g)(2)(B)(iii) (src:393)
GIVEN `the resource is a mobile home` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the resource is used primarily for vacation purposes` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2014(g)(2)(B)(iii) the resource is included in financial resources` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the resource is a mobile home` AND `the resource is used primarily for vacation purposes`
            THEN JUST TRUE  -- the text says yes: "The Secretary shall include in financial resources— (iii) any mobile home used primarily for vacation purposes"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the clause names a class and does not say that a resource outside it is not included

-- src:395 | (v) any savings account, regardless of whether there is a penalty for early withdrawal.
@ref s 2014(g)(2)(B)(v) (src:395)
GIVEN `the resource is a savings account` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2014(g)(2)(B)(v) the resource is included in financial resources` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the resource is a savings account`
            THEN JUST TRUE  -- the text says yes: "The Secretary shall include in financial resources— (v) any savings account, regardless of whether there is a penalty for early withdrawal"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the clause names a class and does not say that a resource outside it is not included

-- src:397 | A vehicle (and any other property, real or personal, to the extent the property is directly related to the maintenance or use of the vehicle) shall not be included in financial resources under this paragraph if the vehicle is—
-- src:398 | (i) used to produce earned income;
-- src:399 | (ii) necessary for the transportation of a physically disabled household member; or
-- src:400 | (iii) depended on by a household to carry fuel for heating or water for home use and provides the primary source of fuel or water, respectively, for the household.
@ref s 2014(g)(2)(C), excluded vehicles (src:397-400)
GIVEN `the vehicle is used to produce earned income` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the vehicle is necessary for the transportation of a physically disabled household member` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the vehicle is depended on by the household to carry fuel for heating or water for home use and provides the primary source of fuel or water, respectively, for the household` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2014(g)(2)(C) the vehicle is included in financial resources under paragraph (2)` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the vehicle is used to produce earned income` OR `the vehicle is necessary for the transportation of a physically disabled household member` OR `the vehicle is depended on by the household to carry fuel for heating or water for home use and provides the primary source of fuel or water, respectively, for the household`
            THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A vehicle ... shall not be included in financial resources under this paragraph if the vehicle is— (i) used to produce earned income"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the exclusion is for a vehicle that is used to produce earned income, necessary for a physically disabled member's transportation, or depended on for fuel or water

-- src:397 | A vehicle (and any other property, real or personal, to the extent the property is directly related to the maintenance or use of the vehicle) shall not be included in financial resources under this paragraph if the vehicle is
@ref s 2014(g)(2)(C), the related property (src:397)
GIVEN `the vehicle is excluded under subparagraph (C)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the property is directly related to the maintenance or use of the vehicle` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2014(g)(2)(C) the property related to the vehicle is included in financial resources under paragraph (2)` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the vehicle is excluded under subparagraph (C)` AND `the property is directly related to the maintenance or use of the vehicle`
            THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "any other property, real or personal, to the extent the property is directly related to the maintenance or use of the vehicle) shall not be included in financial resources under this paragraph"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the exclusion reaches property "to the extent the property is directly related to the maintenance or use of the vehicle" of an excluded vehicle

-- src:402 | If the vehicle allowance standards that a State agency uses to determine eligibility for assistance under the State program funded under part A of title IV of the Social Security Act (42 U.S.C. 601 et seq.) would result in a lower attribution of resources to certain households than under subparagraph (B)(iv), in lieu of applying subparagraph (B)(iv), the State agency may elect to apply the State vehicle allowance standards to all households that would incur a lower attribution of resources under the State vehicle allowance standards.
@ref s 2014(g)(2)(D), the alternative vehicle allowance (src:402)
GIVEN `the State vehicle allowance standards would result in a lower attribution of resources to the household than under subparagraph (B)(iv)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2014(g)(2)(D) the State agency may apply the State vehicle allowance standards to the household` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the State vehicle allowance standards would result in a lower attribution of resources to the household than under subparagraph (B)(iv)`
            THEN JUST TRUE  -- the text says yes: "the State agency may elect to apply the State vehicle allowance standards to all households that would incur a lower attribution of resources"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the vehicle allowance standards ... would result in a lower attribution of resources to certain households than under subparagraph (B)(iv)" (a failed "if", marginal reading (a))

-- src:394 | subject to subparagraphs (C) and (D), any licensed vehicle that is used for household transportation or to obtain or continue employment to the extent that the fair market value of the vehicle exceeds $4,650; and
@ref s 2014(g)(2)(B)(iv), the vehicle over $4,650 (src:394)
GIVEN `the vehicle is a licensed vehicle used for household transportation or to obtain or continue employment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the vehicle is excluded under subparagraph (C)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the State agency has elected to apply the State vehicle allowance standards to the household` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the State vehicle allowance standards would result in a lower attribution of resources to the household than under subparagraph (B)(iv)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the attribution of resources to the household under the State vehicle allowance standards, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the fair market value of the vehicle, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 2014(g)(2)(B)(iv) the value of the vehicle that counts as a resource` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the vehicle is excluded under subparagraph (C)`
            THEN JUST 0  -- the exclusion of subparagraph (C): "shall not be included in financial resources under this paragraph"
        IF NOT `the vehicle is a licensed vehicle used for household transportation or to obtain or continue employment`
            THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): clause (iv) is for "any licensed vehicle that is used for household transportation or to obtain or continue employment"
        IF `the State agency has elected to apply the State vehicle allowance standards to the household` AND `snap1 is definitely yes` (`s 2014(g)(2)(D) the State agency may apply the State vehicle allowance standards to the household` `the State vehicle allowance standards would result in a lower attribution of resources to the household than under subparagraph (B)(iv)`)
            THEN JUST `the attribution of resources to the household under the State vehicle allowance standards, in dollars`  -- "in lieu of applying subparagraph (B)(iv), the State agency may elect to apply the State vehicle allowance standards"
        OTHERWISE JUST (maximum (LIST 0, `the fair market value of the vehicle, in dollars` MINUS 4650))  -- "to the extent that the fair market value of the vehicle exceeds $4,650"

§ `s 2014(g)(3) to (8) Excluded assets`

-- src:403 | (3) The Secretary shall exclude from financial resources the value of a burial plot for each member of a household and nonliquid resources necessary to allow the household to carry out a plan for self-sufficiency approved by the State agency that constitutes adequate participation in an employment and training program under section 2015(d) of this title or a pilot project under section 2025(h)(1)(F) of this title. The Secretary shall also exclude from financial resources any earned income tax credits received by any member of the household for a period of 12 months from receipt if such member was participating in the supplemental nutrition assistance program at the time the credits were received and participated in such program continuously during the 12-month period.
@ref s 2014(g)(3), first sentence, the burial plot (src:403)
GIVEN `the resource is a burial plot for a member of the household` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2014(g)(3) the burial plot is excluded from financial resources` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the resource is a burial plot for a member of the household`
            THEN JUST TRUE  -- the text says yes: "The Secretary shall exclude from financial resources the value of a burial plot for each member of a household"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the exclusion is for "a burial plot for each member of a household"

-- src:403 | and nonliquid resources necessary to allow the household to carry out a plan for self-sufficiency approved by the State agency that constitutes adequate participation in an employment and training program under section 2015(d) of this title or a pilot project under section 2025(h)(1)(F) of this title.
@ref s 2014(g)(3), first sentence, nonliquid resources for a plan (src:403)
GIVEN `the resource is a nonliquid resource` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the resource is necessary to allow the household to carry out a plan for self-sufficiency` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the plan is approved by the State agency` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the plan constitutes adequate participation in an employment and training program under section 2015(d) or a pilot project under section 2025(h)(1)(F)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2014(g)(3) the nonliquid resource for the plan is excluded from financial resources` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the resource is a nonliquid resource` AND `the resource is necessary to allow the household to carry out a plan for self-sufficiency` AND `the plan is approved by the State agency` AND `the plan constitutes adequate participation in an employment and training program under section 2015(d) or a pilot project under section 2025(h)(1)(F)`
            THEN JUST TRUE  -- the text says yes: "shall exclude from financial resources ... nonliquid resources necessary to allow the household to carry out a plan for self-sufficiency approved by the State agency"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the exclusion is for nonliquid resources "necessary to allow the household to carry out a plan for self-sufficiency approved by the State agency" that is adequate participation

-- src:403 | The Secretary shall also exclude from financial resources any earned income tax credits received by any member of the household for a period of 12 months from receipt if such member was participating in the supplemental nutrition assistance program at the time the credits were received and participated in such program continuously during the 12-month period.
@ref s 2014(g)(3), second sentence, the earned income tax credit (src:403)
GIVEN `the resource is an earned income tax credit received by a member of the household` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the member was participating in the supplemental nutrition assistance program at the time the credit was received` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the member participated in the program continuously during the 12-month period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the credit was received` IS A DATE
      `the date of the determination` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2014(g)(3) the earned income tax credit is excluded from financial resources` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the resource is an earned income tax credit received by a member of the household`
            THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the exclusion is for "any earned income tax credits received by any member of the household"
        IF NOT (`the member was participating in the supplemental nutrition assistance program at the time the credit was received` AND `the member participated in the program continuously during the 12-month period`)
            THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if such member was participating in the supplemental nutrition assistance program at the time the credits were received and participated in such program continuously during the 12-month period" (a failed "if", marginal reading (a))
        IF `the date of the determination` AT LEAST `the date the credit was received` AND `snap1 whole months from the earlier date to the later date` `the date the credit was received` `the date of the determination` LESS THAN 12
            THEN JUST TRUE  -- the text says yes: "for a period of 12 months from receipt"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the exclusion is "for a period of 12 months from receipt", and the determination is outside that period

-- src:404 | In the case of farm property (including land, equipment, and supplies) that is essential to the self-employment of a household member in a farming operation, the Secretary shall exclude from financial resources the value of such property until the expiration of the 1-year period beginning on the date such member ceases to be self-employed in farming.
@ref s 2014(g)(4), farm property (src:404)
GIVEN `the resource is farm property that is essential to the self-employment of a household member in a farming operation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the member is still self-employed in farming` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the member ceased to be self-employed in farming` IS A DATE
      `the date of the determination` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2014(g)(4) the farm property is excluded from financial resources` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the resource is farm property that is essential to the self-employment of a household member in a farming operation`
            THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the exclusion is for "farm property ... that is essential to the self-employment of a household member in a farming operation"
        IF `the member is still self-employed in farming`
            THEN JUST TRUE  -- the text says yes: "the Secretary shall exclude from financial resources the value of such property until the expiration of the 1-year period beginning on the date such member ceases to be self-employed in farming"
        IF `the date of the determination` AT LEAST `the date the member ceased to be self-employed in farming` AND `snap1 whole months from the earlier date to the later date` `the date the member ceased to be self-employed in farming` `the date of the determination` LESS THAN 12
            THEN JUST TRUE  -- the text says yes: "until the expiration of the 1-year period beginning on the date such member ceases to be self-employed in farming"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the exclusion runs "until the expiration of the 1-year period" and the determination is outside it

-- src:405 | Resources so identified shall be excluded as inaccessible resources. A resource shall be so identified if its sale or other disposition is unlikely to produce any significant amount of funds for the support of the household.
@ref s 2014(g)(5), inaccessible resources (src:405)
GIVEN `the resource is of a kind that the household is unlikely to be able to sell for any significant return because the household's interest is relatively slight or because the cost of selling it would be relatively great` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the sale or other disposition of the resource is unlikely to produce any significant amount of funds for the support of the household` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2014(g)(5) the resource is excluded as an inaccessible resource` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the resource is of a kind that the household is unlikely to be able to sell for any significant return because the household's interest is relatively slight or because the cost of selling it would be relatively great` OR `the sale or other disposition of the resource is unlikely to produce any significant amount of funds for the support of the household`
            THEN JUST TRUE  -- the text says yes: "Resources so identified shall be excluded as inaccessible resources. A resource shall be so identified if its sale or other disposition is unlikely to produce any significant amount of funds"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A resource shall be so identified if its sale or other disposition is unlikely to produce any significant amount of funds for the support of the household" (a failed "if", marginal reading (a))

-- src:405 | (5) The Secretary shall promulgate rules by which State agencies shall develop standards for identifying kinds of resources that, as a practical matter, the household is unlikely to be able to sell for any significant return because the household’s interest is relatively slight or because the cost of selling the household’s interest would be relatively great. Resources so identified shall be excluded as inaccessible resources. A resource shall be so identified if its sale or other disposition is unlikely to produce any significant amount of funds for the support of the household. The Secretary shall not require the State agency to require verification of the value of a resource to be excluded under this paragraph unless the State agency determines that the information provided by the household is questionable.
@ref s 2014(g)(5), verification (src:405)
GIVEN `the State agency determines that the information provided by the household is questionable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2014(g)(5) the Secretary may require the State agency to require verification of the value of the resource` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the State agency determines that the information provided by the household is questionable`
            THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The Secretary shall not require the State agency to require verification of the value of a resource to be excluded under this paragraph unless the State agency determines that the information provided by the household is questionable"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): once the State agency finds the information questionable the sentence stops forbidding, and does not say that verification is then required

-- src:408 | Subject to subparagraph (B), a State agency may, at the option of the State agency, exclude from financial resources under this subsection any types of financial resources that the State agency does not consider when determining eligibility for—
-- src:409 | (i) cash assistance under a program funded under part A of title IV of the Social Security Act (42 U.S.C. 601 et seq.); or
-- src:410 | (ii) medical assistance under section 1931 of the Social Security Act (42 U.S.C. 1396u–1).
-- src:411 | (B) Limitations.—
-- src:412 | Except to the extent that any of the types of resources specified in clauses (i) through (iv) are excluded under another paragraph of this subsection, subparagraph (A) does not authorize a State agency to exclude—
-- src:413 | (i) cash;
-- src:414 | (ii) licensed vehicles;
-- src:415 | (iii) amounts in any account in a financial institution that are readily available to the household; or
-- src:416 | (iv) any other similar type of resource the inclusion in financial resources of which the Secretary determines by regulation to be essential to equitable determinations of eligibility under the supplemental nutrition assistance program.
@ref s 2014(g)(6), types of resources not considered under certain other federal programs (src:408-416)
GIVEN `the State agency does not consider the type of resource when determining eligibility for cash assistance under a program funded under part A of title IV of the Social Security Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the State agency does not consider the type of resource when determining eligibility for medical assistance under section 1931 of the Social Security Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the type of resource is cash` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the type of resource is a licensed vehicle` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the type of resource is an amount in an account in a financial institution that is readily available to the household` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the type of resource is another similar type the inclusion of which in financial resources the Secretary determines by regulation to be essential to equitable determinations of eligibility` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the type of resource is excluded under another paragraph of subsection (g)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2014(g)(6) the State agency may exclude the type of resource` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the type of resource is excluded under another paragraph of subsection (g)`)
           AND (`the type of resource is cash` OR `the type of resource is a licensed vehicle` OR `the type of resource is an amount in an account in a financial institution that is readily available to the household` OR `the type of resource is another similar type the inclusion of which in financial resources the Secretary determines by regulation to be essential to equitable determinations of eligibility`)
            THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "subparagraph (A) does not authorize a State agency to exclude— (i) cash; (ii) licensed vehicles; (iii) amounts in any account in a financial institution that are readily available to the household"
        IF `the State agency does not consider the type of resource when determining eligibility for cash assistance under a program funded under part A of title IV of the Social Security Act` OR `the State agency does not consider the type of resource when determining eligibility for medical assistance under section 1931 of the Social Security Act`
            THEN JUST TRUE  -- the text says yes: "a State agency may, at the option of the State agency, exclude from financial resources under this subsection any types of financial resources that the State agency does not consider when determining eligibility for"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the State agency's option is for types it does not consider for cash assistance under part A of title IV or medical assistance under section 1931

-- src:419 | The Secretary shall exclude from financial resources under this subsection the value of—
-- src:420 | (i) any funds in a plan, contract, or account, described in sections 401(a), 403(a), 403(b), 408, 408A, 457(b), and 501(c)(18) of title 26 and the value of funds in a Federal Thrift Savings Plan account as provided in section 8439 of title 5; and
-- src:421 | (ii) any retirement program or account included in any successor or similar provision that may be enacted and determined to be exempt from tax under title 26.
@ref s 2014(g)(7)(A), mandatory exclusions of retirement accounts (src:419-421)
GIVEN `the funds are in a plan, contract, or account described in section 401(a), 403(a), 403(b), 408, 408A, 457(b), or 501(c)(18) of title 26, or in a Federal Thrift Savings Plan account as provided in section 8439 of title 5` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the funds are in a retirement program or account included in a successor or similar provision that may be enacted and determined to be exempt from tax under title 26` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2014(g)(7)(A) the retirement funds are excluded from financial resources` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the funds are in a plan, contract, or account described in section 401(a), 403(a), 403(b), 408, 408A, 457(b), or 501(c)(18) of title 26, or in a Federal Thrift Savings Plan account as provided in section 8439 of title 5` OR `the funds are in a retirement program or account included in a successor or similar provision that may be enacted and determined to be exempt from tax under title 26`
            THEN JUST TRUE  -- the text says yes: "The Secretary shall exclude from financial resources under this subsection the value of— (i) any funds in a plan, contract, or account, described in sections 401(a), 403(a), 403(b), 408, 408A, 457(b), and 501(c)(18) of title 26"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): subparagraph (B) lets the Secretary exclude "any other retirement plans, contracts, or accounts (as determined by the Secretary)"

